From fc1b87464496669d8b9c3cd96b330ed12d5146fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:48:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Scope renewal: pin the neighbouring clauses the
 round-4 review found untested

Tests only; no source file changes.

Round 4 (review 6013789432) found no behaviour defect, and 16 single-clause
mutants of the same predicates that the 49 tests did not kill. Two were
fail-open: an uncovered confirmed scope receipt stopped restricting once any
renewal existed, and a deleted mandate comment kept covering.

- New file test_kanban_scope_renewal_receipts.py: really confirmed retain
  receipts (a kanban_failure_commands row in delivery_state confirmed with a
  matching canonical receipt), no reader patched. Covers the safety and scope
  arms of restricted_since, pending_episode, scope_evidence and prepare, the
  episode binding of a receipt, and the uid binding of a mandate.
- test_kanban_scope_renewal.py: deleted mandate, malformed renewal rows
  (version, episode, covered list, mandate reference, digest), episode
  binding of rows, reason and mandate bounds, missing task, orphan
  annotation, writer-kind and creator-task clauses, the ssh marker session,
  ancestry_environs, the gateway notice and the text output of the command.
- test_kanban_scope_renewal_synced.py: Board read-back state/kind/row, a
  reply that does not answer the request, capability shape, and the primary
  push before the Board is asked.

All 13 reviewer probes are adopted as named tests.
